# Roadmap Item 19 — Android release signing template.
#
# This file is a template only — copy it to `android/key.properties`
# (that exact filename, same directory) and fill in real values there.
# `android/key.properties` is gitignored (both at the repo root and in
# android/.gitignore) — it must NEVER be committed. This example file
# has no real values in it and is safe to commit.
#
# See docs/RELEASE_READINESS.md's Android signing section for:
#   - how to generate a real release keystore (`keytool -genkey ...`)
#   - recommended keystore location (outside this repo entirely)
#   - backup requirements (losing this key means losing the ability to
#     publish updates to the same Play Store listing, permanently)
#   - who should hold the passwords (never this repository, never a CI
#     log, never a chat transcript)
#
# storeFile is resolved relative to the android/app/ directory unless
# given as an absolute path — an absolute path outside this repo is
# strongly recommended so the keystore file itself is never anywhere
# near a location `git add .` could ever pick up by accident.

storeFile=/absolute/path/to/your/forge-release.jks
storePassword=REPLACE_ME
keyAlias=forge-release
keyPassword=REPLACE_ME
